h(37, 600, """“They had already sought to cause discord before and turned matters over for you, until the truth came and the command of Allah prevailed while they were averse.” They turned matters over for you: evasion and going round in circles""")

t(37, 1345, """In the floods of Nepal, the idol collapses under the force and power of the water, which draws its power from Allah the Mighty, the One, the Unique!

They made thousands of things, and none of them resembled them. The car did not resemble its maker in structure, shape, work and function! And the computer did not resemble its maker in shape, structure, work and function! Even the robot will not resemble man, neither in work nor in bodily functions!

Every craft man has made has not once resembled his self, his body, his mind, his function, and what was created for him in life such as reproduction and dozens of bodily matters .. Nothing he made resembles him, though it is of the material of the earth; everything he made was of the material of the earth.

Then he made the idol from the material of the earth! Just as the ship, the computer, the car, the house, the glass of water, the radio and a thousand things are of the material of the earth, the idol is made of it, like the ship, the plane, the television, the radio, the telephone, the table, the chair and a thousand things, all of them of the material of the earth! The idol, like them, is of the material of the earth!

The idol shares with all of them in being, like them, of the material of the earth, so how does the Creator create Himself from a material that He Himself created?!!!!

And why do they not worship the computer, the ship, the car, the plane, the telephone, the stones of the house, the paving stones in the streets, the walls, the planks and others? For all of them are of the material of the earth that we tread on!

How can a man stand before an idol worshipping, humble, devoted and abject, when the material of its clay was perhaps trodden on by this same devoted worshipper a year earlier, as he happened to walk, by the decree of Allah the Exalted, in the very area from which the clay was taken to make the idol?!

That is, a worshipper yesterday trod on the clay from which the idol was made today, and then this worshipper, after treading on the idol with his shoe one day, today stands before the thing he trod on with his foot, humble, devoted and abject?!

“Except one who makes a fool of himself”""")

h(38, 400, """Except those who made fools of themselves! Did they see the Creator as being of the kind of what He created?!!!!""")

t(38, 1030, """In my last recording about the verse of the Smoke and the Great Malhama I touched on many different and varied points, and I ended the recording with a final idea in which I dealt with something that is not part of the core of the subject and does not affect it, an idea in which I mentioned a wording that had stuck in my mind 25 years ago, when I said: When the people of Islam see that. The truth is that I reviewed the weak narrations by chain and did not find the wording; perhaps the wording stuck in the mind from the intensity of devoting myself to studying Nu'aym's Kitab al-Fitan 25 years ago. Accordingly, this matter must be mentioned in order to move past the matter of television mentioned at the end of the recording, while pointing out the important indication that came in the Sahih with a chain to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both):

"When it is the fourth day, the remnant of the people of Islam will rise up against them, and Allah will make the defeat fall upon them (i.e. the Byzantines), and they will fight a battle - he said either: whose like will not be seen, or: whose like has not been seen," to the end of the text.

As for nahada, it means rising, advancing and setting out quickly, and this speed does not fit the age of horses, because the narration with a sound chain did not contain the wording that the people of the Levant, who live around the battlefield in the Levant itself, rose up against them; rather the wording "the people of Islam" came, and linguistically it definitely means the near and the far. And the near one coming on a horse will not arrive in northern Syria within hours and reach the battlefield on the fourth day after deciding and taking the decision to move on the third day!

Accordingly, even if all of us do not now have in our hands even a weak text about the seeing, which it was necessary to correct as not having come in wording, because of the importance of the trust of speech and words, and the trust of knowledge, learning and teaching, the saying of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both):

"When it is the fourth day, the remnant of the people of Islam will rise up against them, and Allah will make the defeat fall upon them (i.e. the Byzantines), and they will fight a battle - he said either: whose like will not be seen, or: whose like has not been seen," to the end of the text.

In this saying there is an indication of knowledge, and of the news arriving on the third day, not on the fourth day, since the fourth day is the day all the people of Islam hasten towards northern Syria with zeal, strength, determination and speed, and this is not possible, indeed impossible to happen, without modern vehicles and without their knowing and learning what happened in the first three days. And so, even if I imagined that I had read the wording "the people of Islam saw" 25 years ago, and I see no harm in correcting it, the context of the sound hadith with its chain to Ibn Abbas contains very strong indications that do not at all bring down my inference about the radio or television at the end of my last audio recording.""")

h(39, 250, """An important comment on a matter that came up in the recording on the Malhama and the verse of the Smoke!""")

t(39, 735, """Fleeing from the battlefield on the day of the Malhama .. the crisis and the circumstances

"A red wind blew up in Kufa, and a man came who had no habit (i.e. no custom and no talk) except: O Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, the Hour has come. He said: He had been reclining, and he sat up and said: The Hour will not come until inheritance is not divided and no one rejoices over spoils.

Then he said with his hand like this - and pointed it towards the Levant - and said: An enemy that gathers against the people of Islam, and the people of Islam gather against them. I said: You mean the Byzantines? He said: Yes.

And at that fighting there will be a severe recoil"

To the end of the hadith.

The severe recoil is understood in the sense of turning back and flight, and the cause is connected with the matter of the frenzied, random bombardment of blind projectiles.

And in the hadith, in an important part of it, Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said:

Fleeing from the battlefield on the day of the Malhama .. the crisis and the circumstances

"A red wind blew up in Kufa, and a man came who had no habit (i.e. no custom and no talk) except: O Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, the Hour has come. He said: He had been reclining, and he sat up and said: The Hour will not come until inheritance is not divided and no one rejoices over spoils.

Then he said with his hand like this - and pointed it towards the Levant - and said: An enemy that gathers against the people of Islam, and the people of Islam gather against them. I said: You mean the Byzantines? He said: Yes.

And at that fighting there will be a severe recoil, and the Muslims will put forward a vanguard pledged to death that will not return unless victorious. They will fight until night comes between them, and these and those will return, neither victorious, and the vanguard will perish.

When it is the fourth day, the remnant of the people of Islam will rise up against them, and Allah will make the defeat fall upon them (i.e. the Byzantines), and they will fight a battle - he said either: whose like will not be seen, or: whose like has not been seen - until a bird passes by their sides and does not get past them before it falls dead."

The benefit of this part is that the people of Islam who are not near the Levant at the time this great war breaks out will be saved, if Allah the Exalted wills, from the severe recoil in which a third of the army falls. And perhaps this recoil will be the reason why all the Muslims that day fear taking part in the war in the first three days, staying far from the Levant.""")

h(39, 2400, """The severe recoil in the Great Malhama!""")

t(40, 695, """O stray sheep: your flight into the open darkness has lasted long, and the fallen among you have multiplied between the fangs of wolfish sins, and the gloom of the nights of your grave deeds has covered you, mixed with your breaths, and overshadowed every soul in you.

O rebellious sheep: your clamour against the words of the Lord has grown, and the settling of the breaths of devils in the heartbeats of the sinful men and the sinful women among you has grown great!

You have fled, runaways all of you, not looking behind you even once! You block your ears, wrapping yourselves in every garment you inherited pure, and you have torn it like a harlot who is good at nothing but buying the world whatever the price!""")

h(40, 1400, """The door of the pen is being prepared""")

t(40, 2040, """That you tremble before every person! Even the one you deal with in good manners because you are well-mannered, you deal with him with manners wrapped in intense shyness, trembling and fear of him .. It is not praiseworthy modesty .. It is an abnormal thing, not healthy .. It is sorcery .. That you see 100% of humans with the awe of kings, so you are in awe of all of them .. It is sorcery .. a magician's trick""")

h(40, 2400, """Living trembling before people as if they were kings!""")

t(41, 645, """Walking defeated, turned back, burned from within, like a fortress bombarded with a thousand thousand shells .. Its outer frame remained, but inside it is all rubble, then it shrank into itself, ashamed of the disgrace of its collapse from within!

Walking on the earth defeated .. by the action of sorcery .. It is a magician's trick""")

h(41, 1100, """Walking defeated!""")

t(41, 1810, """Do you know what "the sorcery of separating the eye from the brain" means?

Do you know what it means to live with your eye seeing, but of the image your eye sees only a simple detailed part reaches the brain?

Do you know what it means to see the sea for the first time in your life? To see the street for the first time in your life? To see the buildings for the first time in your life? To see the colours for the first time in your life? To see the sky, the mountains, the rain and the water for the first time in your life?

Then you will behave like a child; if people saw you they would understand nothing, and you will ask questions no sane person asks: Was the world always like this? Was the world always this beautiful? Did you really see things this beautiful all the time? Did people live in the world seeing it like this, with this beauty?!

Then you will walk in the street and look at things .. For the first time in your life you will notice the details of the buildings .. the colours .. the designs that man has made! Then you will understand not only that you were asleep all the time, which will become a certain truth for you, but then you will understand the meaning of the sorcery of the eye!

The jinn settling in your eyes .. sitting inside them and cutting your brain off from the link between what your eyes see and the brain. And if the sorcerer did not succeed in cutting this link completely, perhaps he aspired to cut it 90% or perhaps 95%, under the will of Allah the Exalted. Then you will understand the cause of the scattering of your mind, the cause of your mind's wandering, and the cause of the exhaustion of your mind""")

t(42, 60, """that is constant, the cause of the tightness of your chest that does not leave you, and the cause of your failure to notice the thousands of details around you that people perceive every day with ease. Those details you did not see; you did not see them because the details of what your eyes see do not reach the brain at all. Your eye sees, but your mind does not see; your mind does not see!

Seeing and witnessing are not only by the eye; there must be the cord that links the eye to the brain, and the cutting of this cord means:
🔴 A brain asleep between 70% and 90% always
🔴 An eye that sees only the overall image and does not see the details. Not only does it not notice the details, it does not see them, or perceive their existence so as to convey them to the brain for the brain to notice and analyse them. So the brain analyses only the overall image, because the eye conveys to it nothing but the comprehensive overall image, and it analyses none of the details, because they do not reach it!
🔴 And finally, but not least, a state of constant clouding and veiling over the mind and intellect, to degrees exceeding 95%

In short, it was a death""")

h(42, 900, """If only people knew what it means to live with your eye seeing but your mind not seeing!""")

t(42, 1620, """Allah wipes out sorceries, a total wiping out .. as if they had never been .. as if they had never been""")

h(42, 2000, """Living with "Touch me not": fleeing from people!""")

t(43, 140, """Our eyes were not created to see worlds whose nature none knows but our Mighty Lord, holy are His names and attributes, great in the heavens and on earth. Our Lord created what He told us exists, such as the world of the angels and the world of the jinn, and He, holy are His names and attributes, great in the heavens and on earth, and exalted, highly exalted, created worlds and creatures we do not know. As for what our Mighty Lord made known to us of their existence, they are two worlds dissimilar in creation and nature: the noble angels and the accountable jinn.

As for our eyes, they are of a creation that does not see the frequency. The word "frequency" is purely my own reasoning, and I refer the knowledge to Allah the Exalted, our Mighty Lord, holy are His names and attributes, great in the heavens and on earth, and exalted, highly exalted.

As for the frequency, I lived it and experienced it, and understood it by way of experience; I truly felt its existence. On this basis I speak of reasoning connected to a reality I lived and an experience I witnessed. As for the experience, it was in 2023, between the eye's passing from the state of sleep to the state of waking, a state with its own degrees and vibrations that make it like a daily state every time a person sleeps and wakes. It is not a state that occurs at every waking in the same way, nor at the same level of the eye's vibration and its frequency according to certain frequencies; it has no personal character, that is, it does not occur at all by a person's will, nor by his effort or decision. Rather it is a purely decreed state, in which the eye is subject to a state of vibration that is unusual, unaccustomed, unnatural, sudden, untraditional, not common or customary in the nature of man's waking every day. So a vision of a luminous, angelic world occurs, and the visual sight is cut off immediately with the mere full, complete waking of the eye, meaning the eye returns entirely to its known traditional human nature, which makes its seeing the world of the angels between possible and impossible, as happened to the noble Companion Usayd ibn Hudayr (may Allah be pleased with him) when he saw this scene, and he was not in a state of passing from sleep to waking. Whereas the experience I explain here, I want to show by it the difference between seeing something very similar to what Usayd (may Allah be pleased with him) saw, but seeing it at a moment when a person feels that his eye has entered a frequency and dimension, as if two worlds mixed, the world of the seen and the world of the unseen. The experience was a passage between two worlds, an entry into the world of the unseen in sleep without seeing the scene during sleep, and an exit from the world of the unseen within fractions of a second before returning to the world of the seen, which is the bare human world in which the eye sees nothing but the material things before it. That state I experienced for three luminous shadows in 2023 was a state of frequency and a spectrum, the eye being transferred between two worlds, as the world of the unseen vanished immediately the moment the eye left the frequency it had entered.

This experience is important in understanding the meaning of two worlds existing around us while we do not see them .. The frequency connected with the eye is one of the reasons we do not see the two worlds that are around us all the time.

And Allah the Exalted, our Mighty Lord, is Most High, Most Knowing and Most Majestic""")

h(43, 1900, """The visual barrier and the frequency""")

t(43, 2500, """It is established that the Companion Usayd ibn Hudayr (may Allah be pleased with him) saw the trace of the luminous creation as a sign, not as a bodily image with bodily features. While he (may Allah be pleased with him) was reciting the Noble Qur'an, his horse moved about, so he looked""")

t(44, 60, """at the sky, and there was something like "a canopy with something like lamps in it." The Prophet ﷺ said to him: "Those were the angels listening to you." Here the Companion saw lights and lamps, and did not see the details of the luminous creation of the angel itself as a body.
Therefore the seeing of angels by those other than prophets is an established fact, but not in the great original luminous creation, because this is restricted to the infallible prophets, upon them be prayers and peace.

What is meant by "the lamps and the lanterns" in the hadith is the bare, glittering lights that were moving and stirring inside that luminous cloud (the canopy), not shining white bodies in which the shape or features of the angels' bodies appear as bodies.

The commentators on the hadith (such as al-Hafiz Ibn Hajar and Imam al-Nawawi) spoke about what Usayd ibn Hudayr (may Allah be pleased with him) saw, and said:

Usayd saw something like a luminous cloud, in the middle of which were bright patches of dense lights resembling glittering stars or lamps lit in the darkness of the night.

The reality of these lights: The Prophet ﷺ explained these lights as being the lights of the angels themselves during their descent to listen to the Qur'an.

Why did the Companion not see their bodies? Because the angels at that moment had not taken the form of humans, and at the same time our Mighty Lord veiled their original luminous creation (which humans cannot bear to see) behind that cloud, so to Usayd there appeared only the trace of the light and the majesty of the presence, in the form of lamps and lanterns.

Then the Prophet ﷺ said to Usayd at the end of the hadith: "Had you kept reciting, by morning people would have seen them; they would not have hidden from them." This means that those lights would have begun to draw near, become clear and gradually descend to the earth, until they were revealed to people plainly by day as an extraordinary matter, but Usayd cut off the recitation out of fear for his son Yahya, and the cloud rose with its lights to the sky.

Based on the above, it is established in the Sunnah that this happens to those other than the prophets, upon them be peace, through visual witnessing with the eye in a state of waking, not sleep.""")

h(44, 1600, """Are they angels?""")

t(44, 2225, """Al-Hafiz Ibn Hajar al-Asqalani said in Fath al-Bari that the emergence of the Dajjal is the first of the great signs heralding the change of general conditions on earth (the earthly signs), and that the rising of the sun from the west is the first of the heavenly signs.

He, may Allah the Exalted have mercy on him, distinguished between two kinds of the major signs of the Hour, to make it easier to understand the order of the signs, making one kind related to the earth and another kind related to the sky.""")

h(45, 350, """What did Ibn Hajar, may Allah the Exalted have mercy on him, say about the major signs of the Hour?!""")

t(45, 990, """Yes, and Allah the Exalted is Most High and Most Knowing.

One of our brothers here with us made a valuable contribution in a comment he wrote, and in his comment he spoke about several correct and sound points concerning the impossibility of reproducing internet technology, and he concluded his contribution with the issue of mechanical weapons (machine guns) remaining after the verse of the Smoke, which, as we Muslims have understood, comes before the Dajjal and not after him, stressing the word "understood". Why?

Al-Hafiz Ibn Hajar al-Asqalani said in Fath al-Bari that the emergence of the Dajjal is the first of the great signs heralding the change of general conditions on earth (the earthly signs), and that the rising of the sun from the west is the first of the great heavenly signs. As for the Smoke, as he, may Allah the Exalted have mercy on him, said: (((no decisive proof has been established)))) that settles with certainty whether it occurs before the Dajjal or after him.

For this reason, years ago, in my dream with the Prophet of Allah Isa, upon him be peace, I was shot with a bullet. It was a bullet, and not the thrust of a sword.""")

h(45, 1900, """Will machine guns remain at the descent of the Prophet of Allah Isa? The answer is: Yes!""")

t(45, 2500, """The manner of the prayer of war is known .. Terrorist attacks on Muslim worshippers in prayer places are increasing …""")
